A||N||4||rsuncc||My 87 fiero is stopping on me||||5||
Z||000000||rsuncc||09-03-2001||02:34 AM||||I have a 87 4-cylinder Fiero.  In the past 2 weeks it has shut down on me 4 times.  a couple times while i was at a stop light and the other times when i tried to start up my car.  I have put a new ing. module and crank-shaft sensor in it, but it still cuts off.  It seems like if i leave it set for a couple of hours it starts up.  I have taken it to Pep Boys, but it started up for them and they couldn't find anything wrong with it.  Also the one time it shut down on me, I noticed that it was not getting any fuel when i took the air filter off and look down in it.  But it started up a couple days later.  If anyone has had a problem like this or knows what is going on, please inform me.  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||JetroGT||09-03-2001||03:09 AM||||TCC? Could be a bad Lock up selinoid on your tranny.<BR>Unplug it to check it. If your problem stops, replace it.<p>[This message has been edited by JetroGT (edited 09-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||09-03-2001||02:18 PM||||This could be several things. Start with the fuel pump.<P>When the engine dies, is can you hear the fuel pump running? <P>If you turn on the key but don't start it, can you hear the pump? It sould run 5-10 seconds then shut off if you don't start it.<P>If you can't here the pump run at all then try putting a test light into ALDL terminal G. Ground the other end.<P>Turn on the key but don't start it and see if the light turns on for 5-10 sec. If it does then the pump is probably shot.||||reg||1
Z||000003||rsuncc||09-03-2001||09:34 PM||||I had the fuel pump replaced about a year ago.  <P>It also seems like I am dragging something, like i am pulling a trailer or something, it doesn't seem like it has the same get up as it did before. <P>My car also idles different ways.  sometimes it idles high around 1500 to 2000.  then other times it idles around 500 to 750.  <P>The one time that my car stopped on me the starting idle was around 1500, then it dropped to 0, then jumped up to around 1000 down to 500, then my car stopped.<p>[This message has been edited by rsuncc (edited 09-03-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000004||theogre||09-03-2001||11:17 PM||||unplug the electrical connector on the front side of the tranny and see if it goes away.<P>if not...<P>read all the stuff in the engine section of my cave..... A big vac leak is a real posibility. read the torque strut article as well. it explains why you could have a big leak at the TBI base.||||reg||1
